cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Spatiotemporal annotator: annotate animal video so every label carries an identity and a duration"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ziyuan
    family-names: Zhao
    email: ziyuanzhao.steven@gmail.com
    affiliation: "Department of Poultry Science, Texas A&M University"
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/steven068zzy/spatiotemporal-annotator"
keywords:
  - annotation
  - animal behaviour
  - ethology
  - time budget
  - computer vision
  - poultry
abstract: >-
  A browser based annotation tool in which every label carries both an identity and a
  duration, so a clip yields the proportion of time each individual spent in each
  behavioural state. A detector and tracker propose one row per individual and the human
  confirms or corrects it, including re-anchoring a row onto a different detection to
  repair an identity switch without drawing a box. The state vocabulary, frame rate, frame
  size, detector and spatial zones are configured per project.
